# Design Principles

## Always
- One reason to change per class
- Depend on abstractions
- Inject via constructor
- Fail fast with clear errors
- Make illegal states unrepresentable

## Avoid
- God classes (>200 lines = smell)
- Deep inheritance hierarchies
- Mutable shared state
- Primitive obsession (use value objects)
- Feature envy

## Red Flags
- Class named "Manager", "Handler", "Processor"
- Constructor with 5+ params
- Method with boolean flag param
- Catch-all exception handlers

## Quick Check
Before adding code:
1. Does class have single purpose?
2. Would change here break elsewhere?
3. Can this be unit tested alone?
4. Are dependencies explicit?

